      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Conversation meta is owned by both client and trigger, creating boundary drift and reconciliation flags",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "apps/mobile/src/services/messagingService.ts",
          "functions/src/triggers/conversationMeta.ts",
          "functions/src/triggers/appointmentRequestMessage.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`sendMessage` writes unread counters and last-message fields directly before writing the message document.",
          "`syncConversationMetaOnMessageCreate` also rewrites last-message and unread counters for every message.",
          "The `metaHandledClient` flag is required to suppress trigger-side increments, indicating duplicated ownership."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one writer for conversation aggregates. Recommended: make triggers authoritative for all aggregate/meta fields, remove aggregate writes from `sendMessage`/`markConversationRead` except explicit read receipts, and keep client writes to raw message/read-intent only.",
        "reasoning": ""
