          "apps/mobile/src/state/AuthContext.tsx",
          "functions/src/callable/ensureZenithAdmin.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`isAuthorizedAdmin` returns true when either custom claim OR Firestore `role=admin` is present.",
          "Claim bootstrap errors are swallowed (`catch(() => undefined)`), then role checks continue.",
          "Mobile auth context repeats claim/doc merging, so policy is duplicated across clients."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Standardize on one source of truth for admin authorization (custom claim). Treat Firestore role as display metadata only, fail closed on claim bootstrap failure, and centralize admin-role derivation in a shared auth utility used by both web and mobile.",
